sequenceDiagram
    actor Dev as Developer
    participant GH as GitHub Actions runner<br/>(x86_64, ubuntu-latest)
    participant DH as Docker Hub
    participant IR as Flux ImageRepository<br/>+ ImagePolicy
    participant Bot as fluxcdbot<br/>(ImageUpdateAutomation)
    participant Main as main branch<br/>(GitHub)
    participant KC as kustomize-controller<br/>(in-cluster)
    participant Pod as app Pod<br/>(kanban-prod / kanban-nonprod)

    Dev->>GH: push to main (k8s/** and docs/** paths-ignore --<br/>a Flux tag-bump commit never re-triggers this workflow)

    GH->>GH: setup, run-tests (./gradlew test, spotlessCheck)
    Note over GH: run-tests gates every job below

    par build-and-push-docker-image (needs: [setup, run-tests])
        GH->>GH: derive tag main-<run_number>-<sha7><br/>(D-15's sortable scheme -- ImagePolicy needs<br/>numerical ordering, a bare sha7 cannot sort)
        GH->>DH: build linux/amd64 natively, push BOTH tags<br/>(app + app-nonprod repos, one build, one manifest write each)
    and flyway-verify / flyway-verify-nonprod (needs: [setup, run-tests])
        GH->>GH: open a raw SSH connection, host-key pinned<br/>by fingerprint (no appleboy/* action, D-14/D-15)
        GH->>Pod: SSH forward to the postgres ClusterIP --<br/>Flyway CLI container `migrate` applies this<br/>commit's migrations to the REAL database now --<br/>before the new image ever reaches the cluster
    end

    Note over GH,DH: deploys are pull-based GitOps (D-14) --<br/>this workflow ends at image push. No deploy-to-netcup,<br/>no register-schemas-production job exists anymore.

    IR->>DH: poll every 5m, list tags matching<br/>^main-(?P<num>[0-9]+)-[a-f0-9]{7}$
    IR->>IR: ImagePolicy resolves the numerically<br/>highest tag as Latest

    Bot->>IR: poll every 5m for a policy change
    Bot->>Main: commit "chore(flux): bump images"<br/>(author fluxcdbot@users.noreply.github.com),<br/>Setters-strategy edit to k8s/overlays/*/kustomization.yaml
    Note over Bot,Main: k8s/** is in deploy.yml's paths-ignore --<br/>this commit does NOT trigger a new CI run

    KC->>Main: poll GitRepository every interval,<br/>SSH deploy key
    KC->>KC: render kustomization, detect the new<br/>image tag setter value changed
    KC->>Pod: apply -- Deployment strategy Recreate<br/>(not RollingUpdate, keeps one app pod's<br/>memory envelope steady)

    Pod->>Pod: initContainer register-schemas runs first<br/>(same AvroSchemaRegistrar invocation deploy.yml's<br/>old register-schemas-production job proved,<br/>now in-cluster, ordered by the kubelet's own<br/>initContainer contract -- a failing init blocks<br/>the app container from starting at all)
    Pod->>Pod: app container starts once register-schemas<br/>exits 0 -- startupProbe/readinessProbe against<br/>/api/actuator/health gate traffic

    Note over KC,Pod: prod and nonprod reconcile independently<br/>(separate Kustomizations, separate overlays, D-16) --<br/>a nonprod-only image bump never touches prod's pod
